{"role":"assistant","content":"Reproduced exactly as the log shows. Root cause is clear: `similarity()` returns a Python `float` (`src/app.py:30`), and `related()` puts it into `item[\"similar\"][*][\"score\"]`. boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats — only `Decimal` is allowed. The first publish succeeds because the library is empty, so `similar` is `[]` and no float ever reaches `put_item`. Every publish after that computes a non-empty `similar` list with float scores and blows up.\n\nNow the fix — convert to `Decimal` at the source, plus a scrub in `publish()` so no float can ever reach `put_item` again:","tool_calls":[{"type":"function","id":"tool_SB8j4QXlehXEXjL3SbMUjODp","function":{"name":"Edit","arguments":"{\"path\":\"src/app.py\",\"old_string\":\"import json\\nimport logging\\nimport re\\nimport time\",\"new_string\":\"import json\\nimport logging\\nimport re\\nimport time\\nfrom decimal import Decimal\"}"}}]}
