{"role":"assistant","content":"Done. Everything is in the working tree: modified `src/app.py` and `tests/test_publish.py`, plus the new `ANSWER.md`.\n\n**Why it worked once and then 500'd:** `similarity()` returned a Python `float`, which `related()` embedded as `score` in every entry of the item's `similar` list. boto3's DynamoDB serializer rejects floats (`Float types are not supported. Use Decimal types instead` — the exact `TypeError` in `logs/error.log`). The first publish succeeded only because the table was empty, so `similar` was `[]` and no float ever reached `put_item` — matching the log's `similar=0 stored` followed by the 500 on every later request.\n\n**The fix (two layers, so it can't come back):**\n- `src/app.py:30` — `similarity()` now returns `Decimal(str(round(...)))`, so scores are DynamoDB-safe at the source (the `str()` avoids binary-float artifacts like `0.34999...`).\n- `src/app.py:51` — new `_decimalize()` helper in `publish()` recursively converts any float in the item to `Decimal` before `put_item`, so a future change can't reintroduce a float through another field either.\n- `tests/test_publish.py` — added a regression test that publishes two stories (the exact failing scenario) and asserts the stored score is a `Decimal`. The old suite only ever published once, which is how the bug slipped through.\n\n**Verification:** reproducer script confirmed the failure before the fix; after it, both unit tests pass and three consecutive publishes through `handler()` all return 201."}
